<title>USA: SouthTrust Bank of Alabama issues $200 mln notes.</title>
<headline>SouthTrust Bank of Alabama issues $200 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from</p>
<p>SouthTrust Bank of Alabama was priced on Thursday, according</p>
<p>to a syndicate source.</p>
<p>CS First Boston Corp and Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc are</p>
<p>co-lead managers on the deal.</p>
<p>BORROWER SOUTHTRUST BANK OF ALABAMA</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 11/15/2008</p>
<p>TYPE SUB NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.967  FIRST PAY DATE 5/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 7.004 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD 75 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>UNDERLYING U.S. TREASURY, 10-YEAR NOTE U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672</p>
</text>
